  "comments": [
    {
      "position": 0,
      "source_id": null,
      "text": "だらけ refers to bad things or objects, such as \"mistakes,\" \"garbage,\" etc. It is only used after nouns, but can be used in one of two ways.\n\nN + だらけ\n1. 「Aは(が)Bだらけだ」:　部屋はゴミだらけだ。\n2. 「BだらけのA」: ゴミだらけの部屋\n*Note that the 2nd use is not a complete sentence.",
      "html": "だらけ refers to bad things or objects, such as \"mistakes,\" \"garbage,\" etc. It is only used after nouns, but can be used in one of two ways.<br/><br/>N + だらけ<br/>1. 「Aは(が)Bだらけだ」:　部屋はゴミだらけだ。<br/>2. 「BだらけのA」: ゴミだらけの部屋<br/>*Note that the 2nd use is not a complete sentence.",
      "credits_raw": "rubyhatchet",
      "content_sha256": "cef00237cd3e65ec79ae191661998742bdea7945ccde76d7a1dc15592e0f2c3c",
      "original_created_at": null,
      "original_updated_at": null
    },
    {
      "position": 1,
      "source_id": null,
      "text": "Generally used with negative nuance",
      "html": "Generally used with negative nuance",
      "credits_raw": "Amatuka",
